* claws5_cap -- ABLATION POINT B (FINDING s199 ladder): claws5-match + 3 conditional-assignment
* captures, NO callout, NO table.  Reconstructed by row `callout-fragment-entry-cost` (s199's own
* `claws5-cap`/`claws5-call` witnesses were minted as throwaway, never checked in -- this file and
* its `claws5_call.sno` sibling are a literal, minimal, one-ingredient-at-a-time rebuild off the
* checked-in `claws5-match.sno` endpoint, so the D-vs-B asm diff isolates exactly the callout.
* Grammar/captures copied verbatim from claws5.sno's FENCE alternative, FENCE itself omitted:
* with no side-effecting callout yet, backtracking into a re-tried alternative is harmless (a
* capture write is idempotent), so nothing here needs protecting from retry -- unlike point D/C.
* input: claws5.dat on stdin (runner redirects <family>.dat).  check = SIZE(ZSRC), same contract
* as claws5-match.sno, so A/B/D are check-comparable and only C (the table build) differs.
        &TRIM   =   0
        claws   =   POS(0)
+                   ARBNO(
+                     ( (SPAN('0123456789') . num) '_CRD :_PUN'
+                     | (NOTANY('_') BREAK('_')) . wrd
+                       '_'
+                       (ANY(&UCASE) SPAN('0123456789' &UCASE)) . tag
+                     )
+                     SPAN(' ' CHAR(10))
+                   )
+                   RPOS(0)
        &STLIMIT =  -1
        ZCHK    =   1
        ZBUD    =   1000
        ZFLR    =   20
        INPUT(.INPUT, 9, '[-f0 -r4194304]')
        ZSRC    =   INPUT
        DEFINE('ZBODY(ZKN)')                            :(ZBODY_END)
ZBODY   ZI      =   1
ZBL     ZSRC    ?   claws                               :F(ZBAD)
        ZI      =   LT(ZI, ZKN) ZI + 1                  :S(ZBL)
        ZBODY   =   SIZE(ZSRC)                          :(RETURN)
ZBAD    ZBODY   =   'MATCH-FAILED'                      :(RETURN)
ZBODY_END
-INCLUDE '../../benchmarks/snobol4/harness.inc'
